[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  rocket League was a phenomenon when it  debuted in 2015 and two years later it  shows no signs of slowing down the  unorthodox sports game is a mix of  soccer and vehicular acrobatics that's  immediately engaging but a high skill  ceiling ensures that you can put  hundreds of hours into rocket League and  continue to improve your control of her  car and ball lake in our original review  editor miguel concepción said the  promising concept of combining two  wonderful things cars and soccer is  equally magnificent in execution it's  unique it's complex and now that it's on  switch it's wonderfully portable rocket  league makes the leap to handheld  courtesy of developer panic button the  same team responsible for the  respectable switchport of doom and  similar to that conversion rocket  leagues visuals have been somewhat  stripped down to maintain a steady frame  rate under switches hardware limitations  the impact of the downgraded visuals can  be seen in the games jagged edges and  fluctuating texture resolutions but  unlike a game that relies on a world to  set the stage for characters and  narrative events rocket leagues switch  scars are easily overlooked  the only time when they may interfere is  when playing handheld where jagged  models make it occasionally difficult to  differentiate between objects in the  foreground and background on switches  small display this thankfully is rarely  an issue when you're focused on a  handful of other drivers and protecting  your goal from a fast-moving ball  jaggies are the least of your concerns  and when subconsciously calculating your  trajectory as you ramp up onto a wall  and blast your Rockets for a last-minute  boost to slam a ball into the back of a  goal from midair you probably aren't  focused on a blurry texture here or  there  block a league on switch isn't always a  pretty game but that doesn't stop it  from being every bit as exciting and  competitive as it is on other platforms  as someone who's spent upwards of 200  hours with other versions of rocket  League I was pleased to find that  jumping into matches on switch was just  as easy as before in terms of both  matchmaking and controlling my car in  the field thanks in part to the  rock-solid frame rate the decreased  visual fidelity stood out in fleeting  moments but so too did the Mario and  Metroid cars that I unlocked  he's a Nintendo exclusive rise and their  series appropriate sound effects or  small touches that make the switch  version feel slightly more special than  it otherwise would have this also goes  for the local split-screen play relative  to the constraints of playing on a small  screen it works as well as you'd hope to  say nothing of the surprising  effectiveness of controlling your car  with a mere single joique on it's small  but it gets the job done  makes to Microsoft's cooperation and  developers psionics is handy work switch  players can engage in cross network play  with a wide majority of rocket leagues  existing community as evidence during  our pre-launch tests this system works  without a hitch and matches are readily  available the one notable caveat when it  comes to playing online with others is  that creating custom messages mid-match  is less convenient than usual this is  because toggling chat brings up a window  that takes up the entire screen leaving  you without the usual live feed that  runs in the background in other versions  of the game you do have the option of  connecting a USB keyboard if you want to  type out messages while your switch is  docked which can help speed up the  process save for its presentation rocket  League on switches every bit the game it  is elsewhere and when you factor in its  newfound portability it's also the most  versatile that alone makes it attractive  to regular rocket League competitors for  people new to the game they have a lot  to look forward to regardless as rocket  League is one of the most fascinating  sports games in memory never mind if you  don't like soccer or could care less  about the games growing eSports  community rocket league is a unique game  that redefines the concepts of what a  sports game can be and psionics  continues to support it with new content  on a regular basis it's been around for  a while but now that rocket League is on  switch there's no better time to give it  a shot  [Music]

